{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["macOS"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"text":"TaskPriority","kind":"identifier"}],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"content":[{"level":2,"text":"Overview","anchor":"overview","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The executor determines how priority information affects the way tasks are scheduled."},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"The behavior varies depending on the executor currently being used."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"Typically, executors attempt to run tasks with a higher priority","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"before tasks with a lower priority.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"However, the semantics of how priority is treated are left up to each","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"platform and ","type":"text"},{"code":"Executor","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" implementation."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Child tasks automatically inherit their parent task’s priority."},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Detached tasks created by ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"detach(priority:operation:)"},{"text":" don’t inherit task priority","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"because they aren’t attached to the current task."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"In some situations the priority of a task is elevated —"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"that is, the task is treated as it if had a higher priority,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"without actually changing the priority of the task:","type":"text"}]},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"If a task runs on behalf of an actor,","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and a new higher-priority task is enqueued to the actor,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"then the actor’s current task is temporarily elevated"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"to the priority of the enqueued task.","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"This priority elevation allows the new task","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"to be processed at the priority it was enqueued with."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"If a higher-priority task calls the ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"get()"},{"text":" method,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"then the priority of this task increases until the task completes."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"In both cases, priority elevation helps you prevent a low-priority task","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"from blocking the execution of a high priority task,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"which is also known as "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"priority inversion","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]}],"kind":"content"}],"topicSections":[{"title":"Operators","generated":true,"anchor":"Operators","identifiers":["doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/TaskPriority\/!=(_:_:)"]},{"generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/TaskPriority\/init(_:)","doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/TaskPriority\/init(rawValue:)"],"title":"Initializers","anchor":"Initializers"},{"generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/TaskPriority\/rawValue-swift.property"],"title":"Instance Properties","anchor":"Instance-Properties"},{"generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/TaskPriority\/RawValue-swift.typealias"],"title":"Type Aliases","anchor":"Type-Aliases"},{"title":"Type Properties","g